@krusch/toolkit replaces regenerated boilerplate with a compounding catalog of pre-audited Golden Bricks across Node 22 TypeScript, Python, React, and Cloudflare Workers—snapping in 5 lines for DNS-pinned SSRF fetch, idempotency locks, SHA-256 audit logs, RBAC, or signed cursors.

3
00:00:49,133 --> 00:01:16,825
With krusch-lego, stamping any of 7 production blueprints takes <50ms and 0 LLM tokens. And the catalog never bloats: lego-scout enforces the Rule-of-3, promoting a pattern into a Golden Brick only after it proves itself across >=3 real repositories.

4
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:40,747
Every commit passes through a <1ms, zero-token Slop Breaker. 16 deterministic detectors catch hand-rolled servers, unclamped ORM pagination, outbound SSRF, mutable audit tables, and hardcoded secret fallbacks—redirecting the agent to the exact Golden Brick import.

